Another day working for Licorich Inc. Number one in candy. Number one in surprise layoffs.
This morning you got called into a meeting. There were donuts on the table. Always a bad sign.
Jennifer: Sit. Have a donut. We're restructuring.
Jennifer: Good news, there's one position left. It's overseas and slightly sandy...
Jennifer: We can assign you to it, or you can pack your bags.
-> Where do I sign?
    You signed before she finished the sentence.
-> I'll pack my bags.
    Jennifer: Great, you'll need them. The flight's at six.
    She slides the contract over. Somehow it's already signed.
Two flights and one very bumpy jeep ride later, you're standing in the sand. Your phone rings before your feet stop sinking.
Jennifer: You made it. Look around. Take it all in.
Jennifer: That shack is your office. And your factory. And your bedroom. You can infer the rest.
Jennifer: The stall out front is where desserts turn into money. That's the only part I care about.
Jennifer: Those three girls in aprons are your workforce. They think they'll be getting paid for baking. Let's not ruin that for them.
Jennifer: And yes, the ground is made of dessert. Cake, cookie dough, ice cream. Legal says don't ask, so don't ask.
-> Why is the ground made of dessert?
    Jennifer: What did I *just* say? #scolding
-> Got it. No questions.
    Jennifer: Look at that, you're learning already.
Jennifer: Hit your numbers and you keep your job. Hit them hard enough and we'll talk about a promotion.
<<jump Game_Start>>
===
